INT. MATTRESS SHOWROOM - MIDNIGHT

Rows of beds under spotlights. A banner: "24-HOUR SLEEP-OFF!" A single clock ticks.

WANDA (50s, silk robe, sleep mask pushed up) lies stiffly on a king-size, hands folded like a corpse. GUS (60s, store manager, tie loosened) hovers with a clipboard. KIT (20s, intern, pajama pants) kneels at the bedside holding a tiny stopwatch.

GUS
Wanda, you've been lying there for nineteen hours.

WANDA
Eighteen hours, forty minutes, Gus.

KIT
She's right. I've been counting.

GUS
Kit, you shouldn't be encouraging her.

KIT
She's very peaceful, Mr. Gus.

WANDA
The prize is a lifetime supply of pillows.

GUS
It's one pillow. You'd get one pillow.

WANDA
A good pillow.

Gus sighs. Sits on the next mattress. Yawns. Kit yawns. Wanda smiles, eyes closed.

WANDA (CONT'D)
Gus, dear. Don't lie down.

GUS
I'm just resting my back.

KIT
Mr. Gus, you're horizontal.

GUS
I'm... diagonal.

Wanda sits up with a crisp snap. Pulls a gleaming trophy from under the sheets.

WANDA
Three days ago I faked that bed rule. The contest only requires you to stay in the store.

GUS
You were never asleep?

WANDA
Not for a second.

Kit slumps to the floor, snoring.
